  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You’re given a sequence AAA of size NNN. Your task is to choose a non-empty subsequence BBB of AAA to maximize f(B)f(B)f(B).\n\nHere, f(B)f(B)f(B) is defined as ∣B∣+gcd(B1,B2,…,B∣B∣)|B|+gcd(B_1,B_2,\\ldots,B_{|B|})∣B∣+gcd(B1​,B2​,…,B∣B∣​), where ∣B∣|B|∣B∣ is the size of BBB and gcd(B1,B2,…,B∣B∣)gcd(B_1,B_2,\\ldots,B_{|B|})gcd(B1​,B2​,…,B∣B∣​) is the greatest common divisor of all numbers in BBB.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,⋯ ,ANA_1,A_2,\\cdots,A_NA1​,A2​,⋯,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line - the maximum value of f(B)f(B)f(B).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤4⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 4 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤4⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤10121 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^{12}1≤Ai​≤1012",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 4⋅1054 \\cdot 10^54⋅105."
    ],
